    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d831">

                <pb facs="0953" n="941" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg941"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/31290</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Apostolic Delegate at Washington</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cicognani</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Under
                        Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 492/42</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-10">August 10,
                        1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Welles</hi>: Allow me to thank you most
                    kindly for your esteemed communication of August 8th with reference to the
                    proposed declaration of Rome as an open city. The contents of your message were
                    immediately transmitted to the Cardinal Secretary of State. I shall be honored
                    to present any further considerations on this matter which His Eminence may
                    eventually transmit.</p>
                <p>Assuring you of my deep appreciation of your prompt reply to my letter of August
                    7th, and with sentiments of high personal regard [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. G. Cicognani</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Archbishop of Laodicea</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
